# Code owners (v1.0.4 P4-03). GitHub can only name accounts; the team roles behind each line are in the comment.
# The repo has one GitHub account (the owner), so "Require review from Code Owners" stays OFF (GitHub does not let
# the owner approve their own PR). These lines are a GUIDE, not a gate (SEC FB-R4-SEC-OPS-V104-05). The gate is:
#   (a) pinned tests (e.g. PINNED_SELF_DATA_FIELDS in serializer.test.ts) – which is why the test files are SEC too;
#   (b) ORC before merging: `git diff --name-only <base>...<head>` against the SEC lines below. Any match needs a
#       rounds/<round>/reviews/SEC-on-*.md that names the reviewed head commit (or a head that differs only in
#       non-SEC files), concludes ĐẠT / ĐẠT CÓ ĐK, with every Blocker/Major closed. The merge commit names that file.
#   (c) ORC, same step: a NEW migration that disables a trigger, changes grants or roles, touches row level security
#       or a policy, or adds a SECURITY DEFINER function needs that SEC file too, although migrations have no line here
#       (the rule of 0094 and PN-01; SEC FB-R4-SEC-OPS-P403-01, ARC P403-08 – case-insensitive). Only real role
#       statements count and added comment lines are skipped (SEC FB-R4-SEC-OPS-P403-02: a bare `ROLE ` matched
#       column names and the "-- Runs as ottimo_owner (SET ROLE …)" comment of 19 files). Also SET LOCAL / RESET
#       ROLE, SESSION AUTHORIZATION, session_replication_role (switches non-ALWAYS triggers off, PN-01 and 0094
#       included) and OWNER TO (an owner skips RLS unless FORCE) – SEC FB-R4-SEC-OPS-P404R1-01. Check:
#         git diff <base>...<head> -- '**/migrations/*.sql' | grep -E '^\+' | grep -vE '^\+\+\+ |^\+[[:space:]]*--' \
#           | grep -iE 'DISABLE TRIGGER|GRANT|REVOKE|ROW LEVEL SECURITY|POLICY|SECURITY DEFINER|OWNER[[:space:]]+TO|SESSION[[:space:]]+AUTHORIZATION|session_replication_role|(CREATE|ALTER|DROP|SET|RESET)[[:space:]]+((LOCAL|SESSION)[[:space:]]+)?ROLE'
#       A statement split over lines or built in EXECUTE still slips through: this reminds the reviewer, it does not
#       replace reading the migration.
# Revisit "Require review from Code Owners" once the repo has a second account (CI machine, operator).
# Last matching pattern wins: keep the specific lines below the general ones.

